  "security_implications": "The FSM gates data_hw_en_o and data_sw_en_o which likely enable key-manager operations in hardware or software mode. fsm_err_o tied to 0 means any state corruption (e.g., due to fault attack) would silently transition to DIS without raising an alarm, potentially enabling an attacker to suppress error reporting. The mubi4 encoding on hw_sel_i is used to resist single-bit faults, but the asymmetric strictness in abort conditions (false_loose vs true_loose) might be exploited to selectively abort one path. adv_en_i as an abort signal could be a security kill path; if misused it may interrupt a critical operation and leave internal state unprotected.",
